# Backend Testing

Full guide: `docs/testing.md`. Summary for agents:

## Pyramid

| Type | File | Location |
|------|------|----------|
| Unit | `*.spec.ts` | Co-located next to source |
| E2E | `*.e2e-spec.ts` | `backend/test/` |

Run: `npm test` (repo root) or `cd backend && npm run test:e2e` (needs MongoDB).

## Conventions

- Arrange → Act → Assert; one behavior per `it()`.
- Variables: `inputX`, `mockX`, `actualX`, `expectedX`.
- Assert **service behavior** (filters, exceptions, return shapes) — not that Mongoose works.
- **No** `admin/test` smoke endpoints on controllers.

## Unit tests (services)

Mock Mongoose model via `getModelToken(Entity.name)`; mock sibling services; use `createMockConfigService()` from `backend/test/support/mocks/config.mock.ts`.

## E2E tests

Use helpers in `backend/test/support/`:

- `createTestApp` / `closeTestApp` — bootstrap with versioning + `ValidationPipe`
- `clearDatabase` — between tests
- `seedAdminUser`, `loginAsAdmin` — protected routes

## When to add tests

Add or extend tests when touching a module — prioritize changed behavior over blanket coverage.
